# Email Formatting — Gmail Friendly

When writing emails for the user to copy and paste into Gmail:

- **Never use markdown tables** — Gmail does not render them. Use plain text line items instead.
- **Never use markdown formatting** that won't render in Gmail (no `**bold**`, no `# headers`, no `- [ ] checkboxes`).
- Write in **plain text** that looks correct when pasted directly into a Gmail compose window.
- Use line breaks and spacing for visual structure, not markdown syntax.
- For lists, use plain dashes or bullet-style lines — not markdown bullet syntax.
- For emphasis, just use natural language or CAPS sparingly — not asterisks or underscores.
- Links should be full URLs on their own line so they auto-link in Gmail.
- Keep the tone professional but conversational — match Danny's natural voice.
